    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Metallic minerals such as Iron Ore and Manganese form the industrial backbone of India.",
        "Non-metallic minerals like Mica and Limestone are critical components for the electrical and cement industries.",
        "Coal remains India's primary source of power, while Petroleum is regarded as 'Liquid Gold'.",
        "Non-conventional energy sources—including Solar, Wind, Hydroelectric, and Nuclear energy—are crucial for renewable energy transitions.",
        "Sustainable development requires active conservation of finite mineral and energy resources."
